#chapter-head("Chapter 04", "Dead Drops on the Kabuki Canal", "WATSON // KABUKI DRAINAGE DOCK & LITTLE CHINA · 22:45")

#prose-lead("I")[t didn’t take long for Viktor’s old contacts to crack the batch signature stamped into the glass vial from Northside: `NOX-9-K4`.]

Down on street level outside Esoterica, Misty’s voice returned through V’s holo—tighter now, edged with urgency. An old Biotechnica patent clerk had matched the dormant compound to one disgraced hematologist: *Dr. Adrián Valdés*. Moments earlier, a live telemetry ping from that exact batch had tripped across an abandoned drainage dock along the Kabuki Canal.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_07_kabuki_shrine.jpg",
  "FIG. 07 // KABUKI CANAL DRAINAGE DOCK",
  "Damp votive candles pin down an inverted High Priestess Tarot card—stapled on the reverse with Dr. Adrián Valdés's revoked medical license.",
)

At the edge of Kabuki’s concrete canal, mist curled up off black water lit by neon billboards overhead. Someone had left a hasty triad of clues along the walkway: a scarred white-and-blue portable cryo cooler with its Biotechnica seals gouged off by a blade, an active telemetry relay still blinking amber beside a concrete bollard, and another wet circle of candles pinning down a single Tarot card.

V swept each piece carefully without waking half of Watson. Inside the cooler rattled empty `NOX-9-K4` flasks beside laminated dosing tags for *Subject L-14 (Lucía Reyes)* and *Subject M-09 (Mateo)*. Beneath the candle wax waited _The High Priestess_, hung inverted—and stapled right across her back was the revoked corporate medical license of Dr. Adrián Valdés. Not a worship altar at all: a calling card meant to remind a cornered man that Night City had no lock strong enough to hide him.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_08_kabuki_cooler.jpg",
  "FIG. 08 // SCRAPED BIOTECHNICA COOLER",
  "Empty NOX-9-K4 flasks and dosing tags for Lucía Reyes (L-14) and Mateo (M-09) link Valdés's serum directly to the missing Watson youths.",
)

#tarot-plate(
  "II · REVERSED",
  "Inverted High Priestess",
  "Silence Broken · Valdés's Warning",
  "/assets/art/tarot_high_priestess.png",
  "Pinned between damp candles in Kabuki, the veiled Priestess turns upside-down—not revelation, but surveillance turned inward to terrify an informant into keeping quiet.",
  "LICENSE MATCH // Dr. Adrián Valdés (Biotechnica Hematology, Revoked). Active microwave telemetry relay triangulates directly from Kabuki Canal to a secluded pedestrian court in southern Little China.",
)

The telemetry relay took less than five seconds to lock onto a back-alley pedestrian court tucked behind Little China’s market stalls. V found Adrián Valdés standing beside a narrow metal table cluttered with cold coffee cups, folded notes, and an encrypted shard, flanked by trash sacks and damp concrete. At fifty, with silvering temples, a stethoscope draped like a relic over a sleeveless vest, and cheap chrome braced at his wrists, he flinched hard when footsteps echoed off the wall.

#dialogue-block("Dr. Adrián Valdés", "Stop—don't take another step! If The Cantor sent you to silence me, pull the trigger and get it over with.")
#dialogue-block("V", "Easy, Dr. Valdés. I'm not with The Pale Chorus. I'm here about the NOX-9-K4 batch from Northside—and Lucía Reyes and Mateo. We know your name is on that formula.")

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_09_valdes_alley.jpg",
  "FIG. 09 // SOUTHERN LITTLE CHINA BACK ALLEY",
  "Dr. Adrián Valdés confesses how his six-year-old pulmonary trauma compound was hijacked by Dr. Helena Solís to build The Pale Chorus.",
)

Under the dim overhead strips, Valdés’s story unraveled without theatrics. Six years earlier, he had engineered NOX-9 to save dockworkers and factory hands whose lungs were rotting from Night City’s smog—people who would never afford corporate synthetic respirators. On paper, it worked: boosted blood oxygenation, accelerated cellular repair. In live trials, reactive porphyrins saturated the skin until sunlight or `365 nm` ultraviolet turned every capillary into acid. Biotechnica scrubbed the trial and threw him onto the street.

Broke and stubborn, Valdés sold his remaining patents and culture samples to a colleague—*Dr. Helena Solís*—believing she had the funding to finish purifying the stabilizer. Instead, Solís renamed herself _The Cantor_, opened free nocturnal clinics across Watson’s poorest blocks, hooked terrified twenty-somethings on weekly dialysis drips, and turned daylight phobia into scripture. Valdés kept mixing stabilizers for months out of cowardice and guilt until kids who tried to quit started disappearing in black vans.

Asked about the Tarot symbolism around Esoterica, even the scientist went quiet: under deep nocturnal dialysis, recruits sketched Arcana and claimed they heard a resonant choir humming from Solís’s Badlands bunker—and Solís had fixated on Misty’s shop as if it echoed the same frequency.

V could have jammed iron under his ribs and taken what she needed by force. Instead, looking at a man already hollowed out by his own ledger, she lowered her muzzle.

#dialogue-block("V", "You can still undo part of this, Adrián. Give me your pass codes, the pier coordinates, and your NOX-9 files. I'm pulling Lucía and Mateo out.")
#dialogue-block("Dr. Adrián Valdés", "Thank you for hearing me out before judging me. Take this shard on the desk—it holds the night-shift passphrase ‘The shadow drinks before dawn’, the West Pier cryo terminal coordinates, and my full NOX-9 and NOX-9B dossier. Use it to slip past the UV towers if you can.")

#forensic-dossier(
